{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/260719-redeemed-as-a-b-splat","id":260719,"title":"Redeemed as a b-splat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-19T09:59:25-07:00","id":260719,"title":"Redeemed as a b-splat","content":"i always wondered what a b-splat for prometheans would be like,and when matt said that they wouldn't be making a b-splat for PtC I was a little bit sad. But I've just thought of this, what would happen if the Redeemed was a b-splat. it always felt weird for that when a promethean reached the New Dawn would stop be completely supernatural. Athanors helped a bit but it still wasn't enough. So I have decided to make them as a b-splat. and this is what i got<br /> <br /> When a promethean finish the Great Work, she Transforms her Azoth into Elpis, which she uses to make her soul. But sometimes the promethean doesn't use all the Elpis to make their soul(the ones that remember their promethean lives) and that Elpis sticks to them in the form of a minor template. It didn't make much sense to me that they had a being for every type of Pyros(pandorans are Flux,prometheans are Azoth) except Elpis. a Redeemed has a pool of Azoth equal to their stamina(or their stamina + 5) the Redeemed can spend a point of Pyros to be unaffected by Disquiet for a Scene or spend a point of Pyros and willpower to be unaffected for the day(this includes pandorans disquiet).also the redeemed would be unaffected of the Disquiet of any of his throng mates<br /> <br /> I planning to make to make it like the redeemed alchemist from the core book, also i want to make it that when a player's character becomes mortal he wouldn't become be useless and the player wouldn't have to make a new one, any suggestions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 09-19-2014, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T13:03:31-07:00","id":260911,"title":"","content":"1. Pyros comes in two flavors: Elpis and Flux; that\u2019s why you have two kinds of <i>qashmallim</i>: the Elpidos (Elpis) and the Lilithim (Flux). Azoth isn\u2019t a flavor of Pyros; it\u2019s a quality. To use a very strained analogy, think of Pyros as fossil fuels: Flux is deisel, and Elpis is gasoline. Azoth is the high-grade gasoline that you pay out the nose for. Prometheans are creatures of Elpis, and Azoth is refined Elpis. <br /> <br /> 2. The whole point of the Redeemed is that they\u2019re not a supernatural template; they\u2019re regular mortals. To the extent that they diverge from ordinary humans, it\u2019s no different than how hunters diverge from ordinary humans: both potentially represent exceptional but not supernatural humans. In fact, I\u2019d like it if the rewards that the Redeemed can receive in 2e would be the sort of things that an exceptional hunter might be able to get. <br /> <br /> That said: if you insist on making a Redeemed-based \u201cb-splat\u201d, I\u2019d make it a subset of the Redeemed, specifically a possibility for those who had an Athanor at the New Dawn. The premise is that some Redeemed keep their Athanors when they Redeem: they have a pool of Reagent that they can spend in the same way that they could when they were Prometheans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T04:38:47-07:00","id":262001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/260719-redeemed-as-a-b-splat?p=260911#post260911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To use a very strained analogy, think of Pyros as fossil fuels: Flux is deisel, and Elpis is gasoline. Azoth is the high-grade gasoline that you pay out the nose for. Prometheans are creatures of Elpis, and Azoth is refined Elpis.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book describes Azoth as refined Pyros rather than refined Elpis, though your model is consistent with Pandorans not having a rating in it. But for your analogy, I think I'd go with Pyros as fossil fuels, Elpis as that refined into a working fuel like gasoline and Flux as that de-refined into pollution (both of which require a certain amount of deliberate agency to achieve), and Azoth as an engine or power plant (something even more profoundly artificial, that further refines Elpis to create marvels, but which can go wrong and generate a ton of Flux instead); either way, I dig it as an analogy frame.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said: if you insist on making a Redeemed-based \u201cb-splat\u201d, I\u2019d make it a subset of the Redeemed, specifically a possibility for those who had an Athanor at the New Dawn. The premise is that some Redeemed keep their Athanors when they Redeem: they have a pool of Reagent that they can spend in the same way that they could when they were Prometheans. </div> </div> </div>The Athanor is the way I'd do it too; it's the only thing that I'd consider consistent with being a mortal since most of its effects can be explained as an instinctive understanding of what Prometheans go through, even if the Redeemed doesn't consciously remember it, and a superior understanding of a self that was so-hard won.<br /> <br /> Suggested System:<ul><li>They keep their Reagent pool - a Redeemed as a starting character has 2 Reagent by default, but can buy more for 3 Merit dots per point. Once the character is mortal, or after character generation, maximum Reagent can never be increased.</li> <li>Can be spent 1 point per turn, recovers 1 point per day.</li> <li>The <i>current</i> stock of points, not the maximum, counts as a Supernatural Tolerance trait.</li> <li>One point can be spent to provide a +1 bonus to be unaffected by Disquiet.</li> <li>One point can be spent to provide a nearby Promethean a +1 bonus to avoid being affected by Torment (the Redeemed must interact with the Promethean in some way to make this happen).</li> <li>One point can also be spent to provide a Promethean already in Torment a second chance to resist it; again, the Redemmed must interact with the Promethean.</li> <li>Redeemed retain an Unseen Sense Merit for phenomena related to the Divine Fire; this means they can sometimes sense the proximity of dormant Pandorans, though positively identification is beyond them</li> <li>Conscious recall of the Promethean life is represented by a Merit called Lasting Memory, using much the same system as the Elpis Merit.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T06:47:20-07:00","id":262091,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I totally forgot about reagent. And I don't personally agree that prometheans are refined Elpis, in the books all they said was that prometheans were refined Pyros, nether Flux or Elpis. I always thought Elpis as a goal, that's probably why they named it after a Greek spirit of hope.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: oh and thank you SunlessNick for the suggestions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T14:33:04-07:00","id":262468,"title":"","content":"I'd do it a bit differently: <br /> <br /> \u2022 Redeemed who have active Athanors utilize Vitriol as well as Reagent. They earn Vitriol by pursuing goals related to the nature of the Athanor. That said, Vitriol should be rare for the Redeemed, given its limited utility. <br /> \u2022 As with a Promethean, Vitriol can be stockpiled in an Athanor to provide a Reagent pool. They may not be as efficient as Prometheans in this regard, though: consider requiring two or three Vitriol to be stockpiled for every dot in the Reagent pool. <br /> \u2022 Vitriol can also be spent on Integrity, or on the Athanor\u2019s associated traits. In the latter case, the trait can be raised as high as the human\u2019s current Integrity; that is, if you have Integrity \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022 and your Athanor-related Traits include Strength, you can raise your Strength as high as \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022. You keep the trait rating when your Integrity falls below it; this rule is strictly about whether or not you\u2019re allowed to spend Vitriol to raise it further. This mirrors the fact that when you Redeem with an Attribute that\u2019s above the five-dot human cap, you get to keep it. <br /> \u2022 Finally, Vitriol can be spent on traits representing mortals who are in some way the pinnacle of human achievement: possibilities depend on what the Storyteller finds acceptable, but should include Merits such as Sleepwalker or counterparts that provide protection against Lunacy, Disquiet, or <b>Mummy</b>\u2019s counterpart effect. Other possibilities would be the \u201cHeroic Mortal\u201d Boosts from <b>Strange Dead Love</b>, the Skill Tricks from <b>Mirrors</b>, or possibly even Conviction or new uses for Willpower from <b>Mirrors</b>. If this character has any supernatural resistance, this is how he\u2019d get it; and if you make access to his memories of beinng a Promethean a Merit, this is how he\u2019d get <i>that</i>, too. <br /> \u2022 Reagent can be used the same way that Prometheans can use it, such as fueling the Athanor\u2019s \u201cPromethean Boon\u201d \u2014 the one supernatural power the Redeemed still has (unless you allow him to learn and use alchemy). The downside is that the Redeemed with a still-active Athanor never got the Redeemed Boon. <br /> \u2022 The Redeemed doesn\u2019t count as a mortal untouched by the supernatural for the purpose of driving Pandorans into Dormancy; but he can spend Reagent to trigger the same effect. <br /> \u2022 I <i>do</i> like the idea of being able to spend Reagent to resist Disquiet (assuming the Redeemed isn\u2019t flat-out immune to it) or to help quell a Promethean\u2019s Torment. I\u2019d extend this notion to being able to combat the Wasteland Effect, or even to help other humans combat Disquiet. In all such cases, the expenditure should accompany interacting with the subject in an appropriate way. In the cases of helping with Torment or Disquiet, there should be a risk of the effort going sour and instead redirecting the Torment or Disquiet against the Redeemed. <br /> <br /> Again, this wouldn\u2019t be all Redeemed, or even most Redeemed: most Redeemed would be ordinary mortals, as they currently are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}